# What kitchen-sink's terminal types: the tour of the ten kiosk
# reference screens by keyboard alone, as Showcase's kitchen sink test tours
# them (kiosk/showcase-kiosk-screens/tests/sink.rs). Each `serial` step is one
# burst of keys written to the debug UART's receive side - by NoWayOS's
# tools/qemu-test into QEMU's serial port, by tools/pi-run through the Pi 5's
# Debug Probe - after the screen it waits for. Escapes: \r Enter, \t Tab,
# \e[B Down, \x20 Space. Each screen starts with focus on its first control.

wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
# Start.
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
# A name and a reference, then Next. Every name typed starts zqvj, and the
# reference is 9081726354, both of which the expect files forbid.
serial zqvj\t9081726354\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-choice
# The first topic, then Next.
serial \e[B\t\t\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-checkbox
# The agreement, then Next.
serial \x20\t\t\t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-notice
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing review
# Send.
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing submitting
# The service's answer, as a key: not sent.
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing failed
# Try again.
serial \t\t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing submitted
# Done.
serial \r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing idle-warning
# Yes, I am here: the tour ends at the welcome screen again.
serial \t\r
wait SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
